  - "catastrophic cancellation"
abstract: >-
  Let W(d,t) = (1/2) d/dd |Xi(t-id)|^2 be the transverse Wronskian of Riemann's completed
  function Xi(t-id). Factoring d analytically via sinc_hyp(2dy) = sinh(2dy)/(2dy) yields the
  canonical parity-reduced representation W_tilde(d,t) = W(d,t)/d = 32 int_0^infty y^2
  sinc_hyp(2dy) I(y,t) dy, whose Maclaurin coefficients c_{2m-1}(t) = m L_m(Xi;t) recover the
  classical differential invariants of Jensen (1913) and Csordas-Varga (1990), with
  W_tilde(0,t) = L_1(Xi;t) = (Xi'(t))^2 - Xi(t)Xi''(t). Using positive-weight integral
  representations of sinc_hyp and eta_hyp, we construct division-free Cauchy-Riemann gradients
  and non-harmonic-safe two-dimensional interval mean-value enclosures in mpmath.iv, benchmarked
  on t <= 55 alongside a quantitative Higham |x|^T|y| roundoff-amplification audit of IEEE-754
  float64 quadrature.
